From 4e3085e0a43b57aa2ffe43d206fe2cc694512673 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:07:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 886/913] drivers: stm32_rtc: fix alarm seconds mask test
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The alarm configuration checked "alrmar & !RTC_ALRMXR_SEC_MASK", where
the logical negation of BIT(7) is always 0, so the whole condition was
always false and the guard was dead code.

Test that the seconds mask bit is clear, as intended, so the PREDIV_S
constraint on the alarm seconds match is really enforced.

Coverity issue: CID 1200183: Logical vs. bitwise operator in stm32_rtc_set_alarm
Coverity issue: CID 1200236: Logically dead code in stm32_rtc_set_alarm

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 28ded4041a79215574d1577d14ab7cfadf3cc9dd drivers: stm32_rtc: fix alarm seconds mask test]
Assisted-by: GitHub-Copilot:Claude-Opus-5
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I999893c9f3da1a70e0216b768d1668496b0ff8f1
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/597007
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c b/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
index 0043addda..797c3c49b 100644
--- a/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
+++ b/core/drivers/stm32_rtc.c
@@ -963,7 +963,7 @@ static TEE_Result stm32_rtc_set_alarm(struct rtc *rtc,
 	alrmar |= ((alarm_time->tm_sec % 10) << RTC_ALRMXR_SEC_UNITS_SHIFT) &
 		  RTC_ALRMXR_SEC_UNITS_MASK;
 
-	if ((alrmar & !RTC_ALRMXR_SEC_MASK) && prediv_s < 3) {
+	if (!(alrmar & RTC_ALRMXR_SEC_MASK) && prediv_s < 3) {
 		EMSG("RTC Alarm conditions not met");
 		return TEE_ERROR_BAD_STATE;
 	}
